From 1dad27fcd938d0a6e3ae8ca1adce0766c37b3f53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kv-lend-plan: lend the KV pool's free pages to prefill, plan
 the chunk per request

The KV pool's free pages during prefill. `KT_PREFILL_KV_LEND=1` lends
the pool's free pages to the prefill (pages in use are never lent; the
pool never shrinks). `KT_PREFILL_PLAN=1` plans each request's chunk size
from the memory free at that moment, so a long prompt takes fewer,
larger chunks (scheduler and schedule_batch hooks).
`KT_PREFILL_SWA_LEND=1` sizes the sliding-window pool for the largest
planned chunk and releases its free pages outside prefill. The file
`kt_kv_hot_lend.py` ships here because the plan imports it; it does
nothing until `hot-lend` wires it in.

Numerics: The lend is bit-identical. The plan picks per-request chunk
sizes, so the prefill chunking (and NLL) moves against a fixed chunk.
The SWA lend changes memory only.

Prerequisites: `kv-vmm`, `prefill-lend`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g
